  "narrative": "The discovery pass gives one clear pre-registered effect: SMARCA4 loss is associated with substantially stronger dependency_composite. Because estimates are already signed to the hypothesis direction, R5's signed estimate +0.832 with 95% interval [+0.767, +0.898] means the raw SMARCA4-loss mean is about 0.83 units more negative than the comparator, well above the 0.15 threshold and excluding both null and threshold-crossing values. I accept H5 in this dataset, not as a causal or generalizable claim. I request independent validation of H5 because it is the most consequential accepted finding and could be affected by multiplicity, co-mutation confounding, or technical batch/lineage composition. The engineered marker main effects and marker-by-signature interactions are rejected: all signed estimates are small and their intervals are incompatible with a meaningful effect in the claimed negative direction. Several genetic contrasts are strongly opposite the pre-registered direction: TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss show large signed negative estimates under direction -1, implying raw positive differences (weaker dependency). I therefore keep those investigations active only as post-hoc reversals to test formally, while rejecting the original negative claims. For SMARCA4 loss, I registered stratified and mutation-background-restricted comparisons to assess confounding and effect stability, including adenocarcinoma, adherent culture, TP53-loss-free background, KEAP1-loss-free background, both-loss-free background, and TP53/KEAP1-loss backgrounds. No leakage can be ruled out from the supplied data alone, but the SMARCA4 predictor is a measured binary loss indicator and the endpoint is composite rather than a single-gene knockout measurement; interpretation remains associative.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence: accepted dataset-level association SMARCA4 loss -> stronger composite dependency, signed +0.832 [0.767,0.898]. Original engineered marker/signature interactions are null. TP53 and KEAP1 original negative claims are strongly contradicted by large raw positive effects; reversals registered for formal follow-up. Plan: validate H5; then use stratified SMARCA4 analyses to test adenocarcinoma/adherent robustness and mutation-background independence. Prefer claims with intervals far from threshold and independent confirmation; avoid causal interpretation and generalizability beyond dataset unless validation supports it.",
